  "text": "proprium.feria-v-in-cena-domini-evangelium",
  "about": "The evangelium of the formulary “Holy Thursday — Mass of the Lord’s Supper” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Before the festival day of the Passover, Jesus, knowing that His hour had come that He should pass out of this world to the Father, having loved His own who were in the world, loved them to the end. And during supper, when the devil had already put it into the heart of Judas, son of Simon Iscariot, to betray Him, Jesus, knowing that the Father had given all things into His hands, and that He came from God and goes to God, rises from supper and lays aside His garments, and having taken a towel, girded Himself. Then He pours water into a basin and began to wash the feet of the disciples and to wipe them with the towel with which He was girded. He comes therefore to Simon Peter. And Peter says to Him: Lord, do You wash my feet? Jesus answered and said to him: What I do, you do not know now, but you will know afterwards. Peter says to Him: You shall never wash my feet. Jesus answered him: If I do not wash you, you will have no part with Me. Simon Peter says to Him: Lord, not only my feet, but also my hands and my head. Jesus says to him: He who has bathed needs only to wash his feet, but is wholly clean. And you are clean, but not all. For He knew who it was that would betray Him; therefore He said: You are not all clean. Then, after He had washed their feet and taken His garments, having reclined again, He said to them: Do you know what I have done to you? You call Me Master and Lord, and you say well, for so I am. If then I, the Lord and Master, have washed your feet, you also ought to wash one another’s feet. For I have given you an example, that as I have done to you, so you also may do.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w005", "w006"], "anchor": "w005", "gloss": "Jesus, knowing" }, { "words": ["w008", "w009", "w010"], "anchor": "w008", "gloss": "His hour had come" }, { "words": ["w030", "w031"], "anchor": "w030", "gloss": "during supper" }, { "words": ["w038", "w039", "w040", "w041", "w042", "w043"], "anchor": "w039", "gloss": "that Judas, son of Simon Iscariot, should betray Him" }, { "words": ["w046", "w047", "w048", "w049", "w050", "w051"], "anchor": "w047", "gloss": "the Father had given all things into His hands" }, { "words": ["w066", "w067"], "anchor": "w066", "gloss": "His garments" }, { "words": ["w088", "w089"], "anchor": "w089", "gloss": "He was girded" }, { "words": ["w096", "w097", "w098"], "anchor": "w096", "gloss": "Peter says to Him" }, { "words": ["w100", "w101", "w102", "w103"], "anchor": "w102", "gloss": "do You wash my feet" }, { "words": ["w104", "w105"], "anchor": "w104", "gloss": "Jesus answered" }, { "words": ["w118", "w119", "w120"], "anchor": "w118", "gloss": "Peter says to Him" }, { "words": ["w121", "w122", "w123", "w124", "w125", "w126"], "anchor": "w122", "gloss": "You shall never wash my feet" }, { "words": ["w127", "w128", "w129"], "anchor": "w127", "gloss": "Jesus answered him" }, { "words": ["w131", "w132"], "anchor": "w132", "gloss": "I do not wash" }, { "words": ["w134", "w135"], "anchor": "w135", "gloss": "you will have no" }, { "words": ["w138", "w139", "w140", "w141"], "anchor": "w138", "gloss": "Simon Peter says to Him" }, { "words": ["w145", "w146"], "anchor": "w145", "gloss": "my feet" }, { "words": ["w152", "w153", "w154"], "anchor": "w152", "gloss": "Jesus says to him" }, { "words": ["w156", "w157"], "anchor": "w156", "gloss": "has bathed" }, { "words": ["w158", "w159", "w160", "w161", "w162", "w163"], "anchor": "w159", "gloss": "needs only to wash his feet" }, { "words": ["w170", "w171"], "anchor": "w171", "gloss": "are clean" }, { "words": ["w175", "w176"], "anchor": "w175", "gloss": "For He knew" }, { "words": ["w184", "w185", "w186", "w187"], "anchor": "w185", "gloss": "Not all of you are clean" }, { "words": ["w191", "w192"], "anchor": "w191", "gloss": "their feet" }, { "words": ["w195", "w196"], "anchor": "w195", "gloss": "His garments" }, { "words": ["w213", "w214"], "anchor": "w214", "gloss": "you speak rightly" }, { "words": ["w215", "w216"], "anchor": "w215", "gloss": "for indeed I am" }, { "words": ["w219", "w220", "w221", "w222", "w223", "w224", "w225"], "anchor": "w220", "gloss": "I, the Lord and Master, have washed your feet" }, { "words": ["w226", "w227"], "anchor": "w227", "gloss": "you also" }, { "words": ["w229", "w230", "w231", "w232"], "anchor": "w231", "gloss": "to wash one another’s feet" }, { "words": ["w233", "w234"], "anchor": "w233", "gloss": "For an example" }] }
