    "w031": { "explanation": "“Cena facta” is an ablative absolute with a perfect participle. In “during supper”, “facta” is understood as the meal having been prepared and served, rather than the eating having ended. Jesus’ rising from the table and later reclining again fit this reading. The traditional “after supper” interpretation is also possible. The Epistle and Communion use the explicit “postquam cenavit”: “after He had eaten supper”." },
